 ## Lookup Behavior
 
-Normalize surrounding whitespace and uppercase ASCII letters before lookup. Serial-number punctuation remains significant. Return the snapshot date even when no matching record exists. The concrete index and query path remain open pending the user's choice.
+Normalize surrounding whitespace and uppercase ASCII letters before lookup. Serial-number punctuation remains significant. Return the snapshot date even when no matching record exists. Serials are stored in normalized form under a unique index, so a lookup is a single indexed equality query that reads only files on the kiosk.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index built on each kiosk | On-site HTTPS directory; managed search service | Lookups complete from kiosk files with no runtime network access, as the HLD tenets require. Both alternatives need a network route at lookup time, and the managed service adds credentials and external connectivity. Accepts that each kiosk validates and rebuilds its own index when a snapshot arrives. |
+| Activation | Build into a staging file, then atomic rename over the active index | In-place update inside a transaction | The previous snapshot stays intact and available until the replacement is complete, so a failed or interrupted import cannot damage it. Accepts temporary extra disk use of one index. |
